Data compiled into crate media (include_bytes!). Licence texts are next to this file.

rnnoise.bin
  What: the trained RNNoise 0.2 network (conv 65->128->384, three GRUs of 384, 32 band gains + voice probability;
        int8 weights with a float scale per row for the conv2 / GRU layers, float for the rest), read by
        src/denoise.rs, which ports RNNoise's C code (fft.rs ports its KISS FFT).
  Source: the model RNNoise's build downloads (rnnoise/model_version at commit 70f1d256acd4b34a572f999a05c87bf00b67730d
          of https://gitlab.xiph.org/xiph/rnnoise):
          https://media.xiph.org/rnnoise/models/rnnoise_data-0a8755f8e2d834eff6a54714ecc7d75f9932e845df35f8b59bc52a7cfe6e8b37.tar.gz
          (sha256 0a8755f8e2d834eff6a54714ecc7d75f9932e845df35f8b59bc52a7cfe6e8b37, as model_version requires).
          Converted with RNNoise's own src/write_weights.c, built as its default configure does (DISABLE_DEBUG_FLOAT:
          the float copies of the int8 layers are left out), from that tarball's src/rnnoise_data.c; the file is
          RNNoise's weight-blob format unchanged (64-byte "DNNw" record headers).
  Training data: public datasets only (RNNoise README, datasets.txt).
